          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Are Crowns, Bridges &amp; Dental Implants?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Dental Crowns (Caps)</strong> cover and protect a weakened or root-canal treated tooth like a custom helmet, restoring its chewing strength and shade. <strong>Dental Bridges</strong> fill a gap left by one or two missing teeth by anchoring a connected false tooth onto the natural teeth on either side. <strong>Dental Implants</strong> are small titanium root posts placed gently into the jawbone to support a fixed tooth without touching neighbouring healthy teeth.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Signs You May Need a Crown, Bridge, or Implant</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>A back molar that recently underwent Root Canal Treatment (RCT) and needs protection.</li>
            <li>One or more missing teeth causing difficulty chewing on that side.</li>
            <li>Neighbouring teeth starting to tilt into an empty gap.</li>
            <li>Preference for fixed teeth rather than a removable plate.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
