              <h3 class="mt-1 text-lg font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">X-Ray Guided Root &amp; Bone Evaluation</h3>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">Before advising a zirconia crown, bridge, or titanium implant, we check bone support and surrounding teeth on an instant digital X-ray.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ol class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base text-slate-700 list-decimal pl-5">
            <li><strong>Evaluation &amp; X-Ray:</strong> Dr. Shubham Gupta evaluates your gums, adjacent teeth, and jawbone using an X-ray and discusses ceramic, zirconia, or implant options clearly.</li>
            <li><strong>Preparation / Placement:</strong> For crowns and bridges, the supporting tooth is shaped gently and a precise impression is taken. For an implant, the titanium post is placed under local anaesthesia and allowed to integrate with the jawbone.</li>
            <li><strong>Custom Shade Matching:</strong> Lab technicians craft the crown or bridge to match your neighbouring teeth.</li>
            <li><strong>Fitting &amp; Bite Balance:</strong> The final crown, bridge, or implant tooth is fixed securely and checked for smooth chewing.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
